{"id":"25.05.SplashBlast","contentHtml":"<p>The project grew from a prototype at <code>Global Game Jam</code> into a full-fledged release. Its key difference from analogues is <mark>live physical simulation of bubbles</mark> instead of static blocks.</p>\n<p>As a <mark>Solo Developer</mark>, I collaborated with a publisher and was responsible for <strong>100%</strong> of all aspects: from architecture and shaders to product analytics (<code>Google Analytics</code>) and creating advertising creatives, <code>ASO</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The main gameplay feature — simulation and rendering of physical bubbles — turned out to be a technical disaster on mobile devices. Early prototypes showed <mark>unplayable 10-15 FPS</mark>, which threatened the viability of the entire project.</p>\n<p>The key task was to find a way to render a complex, dynamically changing scene in real-time, achieving stable 60+ FPS even on mid-performance devices.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<p>To solve this problem, I developed a comprehensive optimization system, strategically dividing the load between CPU and GPU, as well as laying a solid architectural foundation.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>CPU Calculations:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>All \"heavy\" physics and bubble state logic were moved to threads using <code>Jobs</code> and <code>Burst Compiler</code>.</li>\n<li>All checks (field state, shapes, move validation, line clearing, etc.) were implemented on <code>bitwise operations</code>.</li>\n<li>To manage performance on different devices, the <code>Adaptive Performance</code> package was integrated.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>GPU Rendering:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>A custom shader (SDF + Voronoi noise) <strong>with physical merging logic</strong> was created from scratch.</li>\n<li>Reduced the amount of data transferred to <code>Compute Buffer</code> <strong>by 75%</strong> using bitwise packing.</li>\n<li>Divided the field into <strong>chunks</strong> and via <code>GPU Instancing</code> pass only indices of the nearest bubbles to the shader, by which data in the buffer is accessed.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Flexible Architecture and Tooling:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>I designed a <strong>modular architecture on Zenject</strong> and implemented my <strong>reusable cross-platform API</strong> for key services (analytics, IAP, saves, etc.), which is used in several projects.</li>\n<li>Based on <code>Odin Inspector</code>, a set of tools for game design was developed: level editor, core mechanics modules, shapes and their collections, as well as adaptive difficulty systems, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced \"Player Feel\":</strong> For creating \"juicy\" gameplay, deep tactile feedback was implemented via <code>Haptic vibrations</code>, <code>VFX</code>, and sound effects.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<p>The measures taken allowed not just solving the problem, but turning the technical challenge into the game's main competitive advantage.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technical Breakthrough:</strong> Performance increased <strong>from 15 to 120 FPS</strong>, ensuring perfectly smooth gameplay.</li>\n<li><strong>Unique Visuals:</strong> The custom shader became the game's calling card, distinguishing it from competitors.</li>\n<li><strong>Product Flexibility:</strong> Modular architecture and tooling allowed easily implementing <code>Adventure</code> mode, and the designed hybrid monetization model (<code>IAP</code>, <code>Rewarded</code>, <code>Interstitial</code>) ensured LTV growth.</li>\n<li><strong>Scalable Expertise:</strong> This project closed the <strong>\"development → data → design\"</strong> cycle for me and allowed creating a set of proven, reusable solutions.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Splash Blast!","date":"2025-05","type":"project","tagsArray":["Mobile","Puzzle","Unity","C#","Illustrator","Photoshop","Audacity","HLSL","VFX","Burst","Jobs","Zenject (Extenject)","UniTask","ZLinq","Firebase (Analytics, Crashlytics, Config, Messaging)","Odin Inspector","Google Play Games","Addressables","Unity Localization","Unity Notifications","Unity Purchasing","Adaptive Performance","PrimeTween","Appodeal"],"heroVideo":["4ZXIa060rTI","OILMjXNu_2s"],"shortDescription":"<p>Led the project from concept to release. Key achievement: created an optimized shader, <mark>boosting FPS from 15 to 120</mark>.</p>\n","storeLinks":["https://grindset.space/","https://globalgamejam.org/games/2025/bubbleblast-0","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.block.splash"],"role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/card.video?v=1765111334065&webm=1&mp4=1","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/screenshots/01.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/screenshots/02.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/screenshots/03.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/25.05.SplashBlast/screenshots/04.webp","width":1080,"height":1920}]}